addr32ValuesSIB00: (SIB with Mod=00 - 256 entries)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
SIB byte format: [Scale:2][Index:3][Base:3]
  Scale: 00=*1, 01=*2, 10=*4, 11=*8
  Index: Register index (4=none)
  Base:  Register base (5=disp32 with Mod=00)

Sample entries showing SIB addressing:
00007476  02000000          dd 0x00000002  ; SIB=00: [EAX+EAX*1] = 1+1 = 2
0000747A  05000000          dd 0x00000005  ; SIB=01: [ECX+EAX*1] = 4+1 = 5
0000748A  01000080          dd 0x80000001  ; SIB=05: [disp32+EAX*1]
00007496  05000000          dd 0x00000005  ; SIB=08: [EAX+ECX*1] = 1+4 = 5
000074B6  09000000          dd 0x00000009  ; SIB=10: [EAX+EDX*1] = 1+8 = 9
...

addr32ValuesSIB01: (SIB with Mod=01 - 256 entries, disp8 added)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
00007876  82FFFFFF          dd 0xFFFFFF82  ; [EAX+EAX*1-128] = 1+1-128 = -126
...

addr32ValuesSIB10: (SIB with Mod=10 - 256 entries, disp32 added)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
00007C76  02000080          dd 0x80000002  ; [EAX+EAX*1+disp32]
...

================================================================================
x86 32-bit Addressing Mode Reference
================================================================================

ModRM Byte Format:
  Bits 7-6: Mod (addressing mode)
    00 = [reg] or [disp32] or [SIB]
    01 = [reg + disp8] or [SIB + disp8]
    10 = [reg + disp32] or [SIB + disp32]
    11 = reg (register direct) - INVALID for LEA

  Bits 5-3: Reg/Opcode (destination register for LEA)
    000=EAX, 001=ECX, 010=EDX, 011=EBX
    100=ESP, 101=EBP, 110=ESI, 111=EDI

  Bits 2-0: R/M (source addressing)
    000=EAX, 001=ECX, 010=EDX, 011=EBX
    100=SIB follows, 101=EBP (or disp32 if Mod=00)
    110=ESI, 111=EDI

SIB Byte Format (when R/M = 100):
  Bits 7-6: Scale (index multiplier)
    00=*1, 01=*2, 10=*4, 11=*8

  Bits 5-3: Index (scaled register)
    000=EAX, 001=ECX, 010=EDX, 011=EBX
    100=none (no index), 101=EBP, 110=ESI, 111=EDI

  Bits 2-0: Base (base register)
    000=EAX, 001=ECX, 010=EDX, 011=EBX
    100=ESP, 101=EBP (or disp32 if Mod=00), 110=ESI, 111=EDI

Special Cases:
  - Mod=00, R/M=101: [disp32] - no register, just 32-bit displacement
  - Mod=00, R/M=100, Base=101: [Index*Scale + disp32] - no base register
  - Index=100 (ESP) with any Scale: Undefined behavior (not tested)

================================================================================
Test Register Values
================================================================================

  EAX = 0x00000001 (1)
  ECX = 0x00000004 (4)
  EDX = 0x00000008 (8)
  EBX = 0x00000002 (2)
  ESP = 0x00000020 (32)
  EBP = 0x00000040 (64)
  ESI = 0x00000080 (128)
  EDI = 0x00000100 (256)

  disp8  = 0x80 (-128 signed)
  disp32 = 0x80000000 (-2147483648 signed)

================================================================================
Segment Selectors Used
================================================================================

  C_SEG_PROT32  = 0x10   Code segment (32-bit protected mode)
  D1_SEG_PROT   = 0x1C   Data segment 1 (writable, for test code)
  D2_SEG_PROT   = 0x24   Data segment 2 (scratch pad)
  DC_SEG_PROT32 = 0x2C   Dynamic code segment (executable copy of test)

================================================================================
Summary
================================================================================

POST E comprehensively tests the x86 32-bit addressing mode calculation logic
by exercising every valid ModRM byte value (0x00-0xBF) and all SIB byte
combinations (0x00-0xFF) where applicable. The test:

1. Copies a test routine template to writable memory
2. Dynamically patches the LEA instruction's ModRM and SIB bytes
3. Executes the patched code to compute an effective address
4. Compares the computed EA against pre-calculated expected values
5. Reports an error if any mismatch is detected

This provides exhaustive coverage of the complex x86 addressing mode logic,
including edge cases like:
- disp32-only addressing (Mod=00, R/M=101)
- SIB with no base register (Mod=00, Base=101)
- All scale factors (*1, *2, *4, *8)
- Negative displacements (disp8=-128, disp32=-2147483648)
